<title>USA: USDA Oct 11 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA Oct 11 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>World grain crops will total 1,830.66 million tonnes in 1996/97, up from 1,702.97 million in 1995/96, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday, raising the 1996/97 estimate from last month's 1,820.43 million.</p>
<p>USDA forecast the world wheat crop at 581.01 million tonnes, coarse grains at 873.51 million, and rice at 376.15 million. Oilseed output was pegged at 256.33 million tonnes, and cotton at 87.46 million bales .</p>
<p>In 1995/96, the world grew 536.32 million tonnes of wheat, 795.02 million of coarse grains, 371.63 million of rice, 255.35 million of oilseeds, and 91.48 million bales of cotton.  </p>
